From df83f1f383d6b0b311459dc162d14c9d84f77032 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Rohr <hey@cyrilrohr.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:22:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] solver: prepare mode=max cache export remotes in parallel

ExportTo walks cache records one at a time, so a mode=max export creates
the blobs of independent stages sequentially. PrepareCacheExport walks
the same exporters first and resolves their remotes in parallel across
independent branches, bounded by GOMAXPROCS. Like ExportTo, an exporter
is prepared before the exporters it links to, which then usually find
their blobs among the ones created for its chain. ExportTo reuses the
prepared remotes through CacheExportOpt.Prepared instead of loading the
results again; failures are still reported by ExportTo, so the exported
cache does not change.

To walk and resolve exactly what ExportTo does, the record loop, the
context selection and the walk over dependencies and secondary exporters
move out of ExportTo into helpers that both use. The record loop moves
as is.

Signed-off-by: Cyril Rohr <hey@cyrilrohr.com>
